================================================================================
PART C  the defect this touch also fixes, and why it was latent
================================================================================
Read the run's own section 5 in PART B against its section 4. Same entry, same build, same seed, same fixture manifest; the
only difference is the flow version, named by hash in each section's own header.

  the flow before this fix   gen_run grades the fixture on a passing sim log and calls it FAIL "red fixture passed
                             unexpectedly". The regression's pre-merge pass then SKIPS the run, because its gate
                             admitted only PASS and XFAIL: its section 5 prints the same result.yaml hash before
                             and after the pass, "rewritten: NO", and fcov_check still None. The check the fixture
                             exists to fail never runs, so the entry fails every regression it appears in, for a
                             reason that is not its declared one.
  the fixed flow             gen_run parks the run as NOT_RUN naming the missing check and records the pre-grading
                             verdict; the pre-merge pass admits it, runs the check (1 declared bin, 0 hit) and
                             grades it RED-OK, and its section 4 prints the two differing result.yaml hashes with
                             "rewritten: YES". Every hash in this paragraph is read from PART B rather than
                             repeated here, so a re-run cannot leave the prose behind.

The run's section 6 is the control that keeps the skip honest: the same pre-fix pre-merge pass, on a real PASS run of the
committed sibling entry with its committed manifest, DID act, setting fcov status PASS over 6 declared and 6 hit
bins and rewriting result.yaml. So the "NO" in its section 5 is a skip of that run, not an inert probe.

The defect is latent, not live: no committed entry carries both red_fixture and an fcov manifest, so no entry in the
tree changes verdict. The first entry to carry both would be the standing guard, and it would have failed the first
regression that included it.

WHY NOT_RUN RATHER THAN THE ACCUSING FAIL. When no stage checks the expectation, "red fixture passed unexpectedly"
asserts the checker is dead on a run that has no evidence either way. NOT_RUN asserts only what happened. It is
visible: the regression summary counts it and never folds it into the pass rate.

