PART F  why this log is retained under gen_tdd_logs/flow, and what happens if it is not
================================================================================
The standing guard's own failing log must be retained here, under gen_tdd_logs/flow, and never under
gen_tdd_logs/lockstep with the family's gen_{group}_red1_stdout naming. The reason is measured, not predicted.

Both loader gates were CALLED on the entry, not read:

entry               : gen_ut_lockstep_icache_ecc_fcov_red
red_fixture         : True
fcov_expectation_file: dv/auto_dv/fcov_expectations/gen_ut_lockstep_icache_ecc_fcov_red.fcov.yaml
red_expect          : fcov expectation unmet: [0-9]+ declared bin\(s\) not hit .*gen_ic_ecc_cg\.cp_ram\.data
red_grading_deferred: True  (called, not read)

GATE 1  the loader accepted the entry: load_testlist returned 103 entries with it present
        (a refusal is a SystemExit from load_testlist, so reaching this line IS the measurement)

GATE 2  red_log_for('gen_ut_lockstep_icache_ecc_fcov_red') -> log=None sim=None harness_prefix=None
        red_signature_check -> None
        so the retained-log replay has nothing to replay and refuses nothing

GATE 3  the fire_id policy fires only on a red_expect naming 'GEN_TEST_FAIL' without 'fire_':
        red_expect contains 'GEN_TEST_FAIL': False
        red_expect contains 'fire_': False

Neither gate refuses the entry as things stand. Now the trap, measured by putting a copy of direction one's own
failing stdout at the lockstep family's path inside the SCRATCH root and asking the loader again:

ERROR: /tmp/claude-1211405897/-localdev-fzhang-ws-ibex-challenge/b61c04c6-06f1-4059-978d-29bc6123dadd/scratchpad/rt35/root/dv/auto_dv/flow/gen_testlist.yaml: test gen_ut_lockstep_icache_ecc_fcov_red: red_expect 'fcov expectation unmet: [0-9]+ declared bin\\(s\\) not hit .*gen_ic_ecc_cg\\.cp_ram\\.data' refused: no collected evidence line in the retained pinned-red log (gen_lockstep_icache_ecc_fcov_red1_stdout.log: harness ''; verdict FAIL: red fixture failed for an undeclared reason: unexplained exit code 1 with clean log; no collected evidence line for red_)
probe exit status: 1

So the refusal is the LOADER's, not a warning: with the log at that path every flow command that reads the testlist
dies on it. The replay cannot see the failure because the failure's evidence is the expectation checker's reason and
not a line in the simulation's stdout, and the message that comes out reads like a stale signature, which is not
what is wrong. Recorded here rather than coded around: the retention location is the fix.

The trap was reverted at once, and the same command run a third time to show the tree is as it was:

